  clock: 3  # 0312
  nonce: '0312'  # 0312
  message: "Fixed in PR #1530 (merge 1a95dd64a2). Root cause: _detect_frameworks concatenates per-ecosystem scanner results, so a name two scanners detect (hardhat: JS + Solidity; ktor: Kotlin + Gradle) arrived twice; nothing downstream (refine_frameworks, to_dict, sketch) deduplicated. Analogue found and fixed: an EXPLICIT --frameworks list with a repeat (flask,celery,flask) echoed duplicates into frameworks and requested_frameworks. Fix: RepoProfile.__post_init__ is the single normalisation point for every producer (auto scan, explicit, refine, cached from_dict): frameworks/dev_frameworks/requested_frameworks sorted+unique, dev_frameworks minus prod, framework_evidence keys restricted to listed frameworks with sorted unique node lists. Evidence on dev after merge (filed repro repo: package.json hardhat+ethers, hardhat.config.js, build.gradle.kts ktor, App.kt, src/index.js): detect_profile(repo).to_dict()['frameworks'] -> ['ethers', 'hardhat', 'ktor'] (was ['ethers','hardhat','hardhat','ktor','ktor']); run_behavior_map survey.json profile.frameworks -> ['ethers', 'hardhat', 'ktor']; generate_sketch '## Frameworks' section -> '- ethers / - hardhat / - ktor'; detect_profile(repo, frameworks='flask,celery,flask') frameworks -> ['celery', 'flask']. Tests: 4 in test_profile.py + 1 in test_sketch.py (red before, green after); targeted smart-test 6706 passed, 100% coverage on changed files."  # 0312
